1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,880
Your fingertips start to wrinkle after about five minutes

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:05,160
in the bath, but it's not just because they're

3
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,300
soaking up water. You see,

4
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,880
your nerves are actually telling the blood vessels under

5
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:12,360
your skin to shrink which pulls the skin down

6
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:15,560
into those ridges. That's why people with damaged nerves

7
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,700
in their fingers don't wrinkle at all.

8
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:19,360
So why would your body bother?

9
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:22,460
Scientists think the ridges work like tire treads,

10
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:25,280
channeling water away so you can grip wet things.

11
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,560
In one experiment, people moved wet marbles faster with

12
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:30,780
wrinkled fingers than with dry ones,

13
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,800
which means your body has been putting on rain

14
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,620
tires this whole time.
